{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363424-how-come-there-aren-t-any-bsd-abominations","id":1363424,"title":"How come there aren't any BSD Abominations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-26T02:06:31-08:00","id":1363424,"title":"How come there aren't any BSD Abominations?","content":"Especially Baali ones. You'd think the Dancers would jump at a chance of immortality and spreading the Wyrm's corruption forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T07:26:58-08:00","id":1363449,"title":"","content":"Because BSDs are still garou and that means their loyalty is to their patron spirits. Becoming an abomination is to spit on those spirits' bans. Nevermind lose their ties to the spirit world entirely.<br /> <br /> Besides, they'd think someone was demoting themselves if they became an abomination, as vampires are very low on the Wyrmish pecking order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T10:56:11-08:00","id":1363475,"title":"","content":"There can be, and they can even earn Renown back, but Abominations aren't described in great number, so it's more that neither Vampire nor Werewolf has cared overly much to spend word count on such an example when there are typically more pressing needs for either one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T20:19:50-08:00","id":1363555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363424-how-come-there-aren-t-any-bsd-abominations#post1363424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially Baali ones. You'd think the Dancers would jump at a chance of immortality and spreading the Wyrm's corruption forever.</div> </div> </div> </div> My understanding is that it's what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> said. I want to say that this is explained in some book or other, but it's <b>definitely </b>the sort of thing that required an explanation because the existence and use of BSD abominations by the Wyrm makes <i>sooo</i> much sense given even a basic understanding of what the Wyrm is, that they basically <i>had</i> to write in a specific reason why there <i>wouldn't </i>be a bunch of Wyrm BSD's. If you look at the language from 2nd Ed. Player's Guide, it seems clear that the Wyrm should love to have some Wrym abominations at it's ready disposal:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;There is only one way to prevent [the degeneration of Gnosis]--the Abomination can fully offer what's left of his soul to the Wyrm. After making the black pact, the Abomination becomes a Storyteller-controlled character. His Gnosis is no longer at risk; the Wyrm sees to fueling his Spiritual energy. However, the Abomination no longer has any free will whatsoever and cannot so much as tie his shoe of his own accord.&quot;<br /> <br /> W:tA Player's Guide 2nd Ed., 191-192 </div> </div> </div> Mind you, the hierarchy of sins for Gnosis degeneration that they provide there is basically a bunch of stuff many BSD's are going to do anyway (warring against the tribes--level two on the hierarchy--is basically the BSD raison d'etre). The 'giving themselves over whole hog/no free will' thing seems like an across-the-board deal breaker until you stop to consider the depth of <i>mundane </i>human zealotry (in the WoD and in the real world); it's not hard to conceive of a person so devout to their god (pick your Abrahamic religion) that they'd give themselves over, completely and irrevocably, to it's/his/her service in a heartbeat. With that in mind, how hard can it be to conceive of a one or more BSD's feeling the same way about the Wyrm? It's not a stretch--so of course they put in a proviso that explains that, even though this line of reasoning seems like it make perfect sense, it actually doesn't, because reasons. It's almost the White Wolf equivalent of the Genie telling Aladdin that he can't wish for more wishes (and why can't he wish for more wishes? Because <i>no</i>.)<br /> <br /> My pet theory is that abominations--like many things in the classic WoD--are a first/second edition thing that all or most of the devs decided later that they <i>hated</i> (just throw them in with the True Black Hand), so they went out of their way to make sure that there was no efficiency <i>anywhere </i>in creating an Abomination, such that the only reason to make one would be as an act of chaotic evil cruelty. My further assumption is that it was probably too much to retcon from 2nd Ed. to Revised that abominations just didn't exist at all, and can't be made in the first place; you can just nuke Enoch to basically get of the True Black Hand, but getting rid of Abominations would require changing the &quot;natural&quot; laws of the WoD, and they'd basically be creating a bunch of plotholes in earlier supplements that featured one or more abominations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T20:55:47-08:00","id":1363556,"title":"","content":"A lot of it has to do with rarity. Abominations are very few, as the great majority of embraced werewolves just die. Even if a group of BSDs could actually find a vampire - never mind a Baali one, who are fairly uncommon by vampire standards - to agree to try a mass embrace of BSDs, there is no guarantee that they'd even get one successful embrace out of it. You could, at best, end up losing up to a dozen or more perfectly good warriors in exchange for one that can't operate during daylight hours, is in a perpetual state of depression, can't regenerate (without spending valuable blood), is limited in using Gnosis, and advances in Rank very slowly. And if the Abomination does pledge itself to the Wyrm, the new Wyrm puppet may run off on its own, as the Wyrm may have plans for it that don't involve its former Hive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T21:41:44-08:00","id":1363557,"title":"","content":"Also your gonna burn through a hell of a lot of BSDs trying to make one. Even the least sane is going to question volunteering for almost certain death on the off chance you end up with something that just gained a bunch of weaknesses with no real advantages right off the bat.<br /> <br /> Or what the poster above me said....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T03:03:21-08:00","id":1363591,"title":"","content":"With Abominations turning out as trainwrecks, which I imagine means all subtlety goes right out the window, it would be exceptionally hard for a Baali BSD Abomination to hide its existence.<br /> <br /> Which means it has precisely fuck-all chance of surviving when a pack of Talons comes at it from one side while the Banu Haqim with an anti-tank rifle sits downwind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T09:04:46-08:00","id":1363636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363424-how-come-there-aren-t-any-bsd-abominations?p=1363475#post1363475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There can be, and they can even earn Renown back, but Abominations aren't described in great number, so it's more that neither Vampire nor Werewolf has cared overly much to spend word count on such an example when there are typically more pressing needs for either one.</div> </div> </div> </div>What he said.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my mind, I only recall one named BSD Abomination. Baba Yaga Embraced the leader of her werewolf armies.<br /> That couldn't have been pretty. A BSD and Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T16:29:21-08:00","id":1363699,"title":"","content":"The only two I can remember were Pariah, the first one detailed in Under a Blood Red Moon (a Ventrue Silver Fang, I think?), and the one from the Black Hand whose name I can't remember (I want to say was a Silent Strider Setite but I can't recall?). But it's been ages since I've looked at Rage Across Russia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T19:46:53-08:00","id":1363726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363424-how-come-there-aren-t-any-bsd-abominations?p=1363636#post1363636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What he said.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my mind, I only recall one named BSD Abomination. Baba Yaga Embraced the leader of her werewolf armies.<br /> That couldn't have been pretty. A BSD and Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poison Tooth, a lupus Theurge. Page 82 of Rage Across Russia details his embrace, but unfortunately no stats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363424-how-come-there-aren-t-any-bsd-abominations?p=1363699#post1363699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only two I can remember were Pariah, the first one detailed in Under a Blood Red Moon (a Ventrue Silver Fang, I think?), and the one from the Black Hand whose name I can't remember (I want to say was a Silent Strider Setite but I can't recall?). But it's been ages since I've looked at Rage Across Russia.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can find at least four garou abominations in books:<br /> Pariah in Under a Blood Red Moon and Children of the Night<br /> Silent Strider Zubeida in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand (no stats)<br /> Allonzo Montoya in Rage Warriors of the Apocalypse<br /> Poison Tooth above<br /> <br /> More:<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Abomination\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Abomination</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 01-27-2020, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T20:09:30-08:00","id":1363727,"title":"","content":"Would a BSD Abomination even suffer from harano? Considering the state of their psyches after dancing the Spiral, I doubt that vampirism-born existential crisis would qualify as a drop in the toxic waste-filled ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T23:22:39-08:00","id":1363743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363424-how-come-there-aren-t-any-bsd-abominations?p=1363727#post1363727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a BSD Abomination even suffer from harano? Considering the state of their psyches after dancing the Spiral, I doubt that vampirism-born existential crisis would qualify as a drop in the toxic waste-filled ocean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of it stems from going from being more <i>alive</i> than any being that isn't half-flesh, half-spirit can ever hope to understand to suddenly being not alive, and being keenly aware on a deep existential level of what you have lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T01:33:22-08:00","id":1364301,"title":"","content":"Yeah, whatever else it may be, the Wyrm seems to be a <i>vital</i> force of corruption. More like cancer than decomposition. The embrace would move the former werewolf in the opposite direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T16:39:06-08:00","id":1364637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363424-how-come-there-aren-t-any-bsd-abominations?p=1364301#post1364301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, whatever else it may be, the Wyrm seems to be a <i>vital</i> force of corruption. More like cancer than decomposition. The embrace would move the former werewolf in the opposite direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>This^<br /> The Wyrm is still a nature spirit, albeit a cancerous one. It doesn't mesh with creatures of the grave.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T21:14:21-08:00","id":1365936,"title":"","content":"As mentioned, BSDs likely wouldn't want to become abominations for (almost) all the same reasons as Gaian Garou. Being alive and connected to the spirit world is deeply important to them.<br /> <br /> With regard to swearing service to a powerful servant of the Wyrm, I look at the total loss of free will and injection of spiritual energy as being something more than just reaffirming their previous loyalty (for a BSD who already serves the Wyrm, that is). I think such an abomination has much of its self displaced by a possessing entity, or at least rewritten like a Drone, and so BSDs both alive and undead would look down on such an option just like they look down on Fomori and rarely choose to become one (despite the power boost).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13544-impeesa","name":"Impeesa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T11:20:36-08:00","id":1366073,"title":"","content":"<br /> 1-You've established a lot of pacts, and they wouldn't like it if you became a vampire. Totems and Rituals would likely cease to work and no future gifts can be brought.<br /> 2-Your ancestor spirit/past life/whatever would be at risk. You wanna pass that stuff on to future generations.<br /> 3-Black spirals have harems and drugs and all sorts of stuff that they wouldn't want to risk on becoming a vampire (Yes, vampires can enjoy this stuff differently, but ignorance abounds)<br /> 4-You can't trust a vampire to embrace you.<br /> 5-You'd feel a great disconect from your pack.<br /> <br /> I imagine you could get around your gnosis preventing you from rising by getting embraced surrounded by silver, depleting your gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-08-2020, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}